WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.202
Hi! In English, a very busy person is as busy as a bee! Today we'll learn similes, collocations and animal words.

2
00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:14.586
As busy as a bee: very busy.

3
00:00:14.736 --> 00:00:18.258
As slow as a snail, as quiet as a mouse.

4
00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:21.666
As brave as a lion, as cold as ice.

5
00:00:21.816 --> 00:00:28.194
Think of what the animal or thing is best known for, and you can guess the simile.

6
00:00:28.344 --> 00:00:34.026
Some words always go together: do homework, make a mistake, take a photo.

7
00:00:34.176 --> 00:00:41.058
Groups of animals have special names: a herd of cows, a school of fish, a flock of birds.

8
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:45.498
Baby animals: a kitten, a puppy, a calf.

9
00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:51.810
Animal sounds: dogs bark, cats meow, lions roar.

10
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.202
Watch out! In English we don't say do a mistake!

11
00:00:56.352 --> 00:01:01.098
The collocation is make a mistake, and the past is made a mistake.

12
00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:07.410
But for homework we say do homework. Learn these word pairs.

13
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:17.586
Your turn! The old tortoise walked as slow as a, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:17.736 --> 00:01:24.738
The snail is famous for being slow: as slow as a snail. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:24.888 --> 00:01:34.722
Another one! We saw a, ___, of fish in the sea. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:34.872 --> 00:01:40.626
A group of fish is a school of fish. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:40.776 --> 00:01:50.370
Here's another! Please, ___, a photo of us. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:56.058
The collocation is take a photo. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:56.208 --> 00:02:05.922
Try one more! A baby cat is called a, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:02:06.072 --> 00:02:11.226
A baby cat is a kitten. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:11.376 --> 00:02:21.594
Try one more! The firefighter was as brave as a, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:21.744 --> 00:02:27.858
Brave like a lion: as brave as a lion. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:28.008 --> 00:02:37.746
Try one more! A baby dog is called a, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:37.896 --> 00:02:43.098
A baby dog is a puppy. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:43.248 --> 00:02:52.746
Last one! Please, ___, your homework now. Which one? Pause and think.

26
00:02:52.896 --> 00:02:58.482
The collocation is do homework. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:58.632 --> 00:03:10.002
Remember: for as … as … similes, think of what the animal is known for. Learn collocations in pairs. Animal groups, babies and sounds have special words too.

28
00:03:10.152 --> 00:03:14.778
Describe your best friend using as … as …!

